SU(2) single-factor first-wall payment peeling obstruction

COMMAND
make -f Makefile.research analyze_su2_aim1_payment_peeling
./analyze_su2_aim1_payment_peeling 30

OUTPUT
SU2_AIM1_PAYMENT_PEELING maximum_level=60 payments=54120 coefficient_checks=16555272 coefficient_failures=2207520 line_checks=16555272 line_failures=2326206 normalized_checks=16555272 normalized_failures=1516034
FIRST_COEFFICIENT_FAILURE level=4 old_factor=1 next_factor=1 label=0 index=12 value=-2 transform_row=[0,-2,-2]
FIRST_LINE_FAILURE level=4 old_factor=1 next_factor=1 label=0 index=6 value=-2 transform_row=[0,-2,-2]
FIRST_NORMALIZED_FAILURE level=4 old_factor=1 next_factor=1 label=0 index=32 value=-6 transform_row=[0,-2,-2]

METHOD
For every half-level through 30, every existing reduced factor,
every proposed next factor, and every first-wall payment row, the
analyzer forms the exact dual payment functional.

First it multiplies that functional by the square of one existing
ordinary character and checks all character-basis coefficients.
Then it rewrites the same functional against the symmetric
unperiodized line coefficient W, convolves its dual by the existing
triangular kernel tau_q, and checks every line coefficient.
Finally it converts the character functional to the normalized-margin
dual by checking the weighted prefix

  sum_(x=0)^s (2x+1) eta_x.

These prefixes are the numerators of the functional on the extreme
rays m_x=(2x+1)1_(x<=s) of the normalized-dimension cone.

Both proposed one-factor peelings are false already at K=2 with old
factor q=1, next factor q=1, and payment row r=0.  The character-basis
product has coefficient -2 at label 12, and the line-kernel product
has coefficient -2 at index 6.  The normalized-margin dual is also
negative, with exact numerator -6 at extreme-ray index 32.  Thus
AIMGP cannot be proved by peeling one arbitrary existing factor and
demanding coefficientwise positivity in the character, line-kernel,
or normalized-margin basis.  The exact first failures, not the
bounded census, establish these obstructions.

COMPILER FLAGS
g++ -O2 -std=c++20 -Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic -Wconversion \
  -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow -Werror \
  analyze_su2_aim1_payment_peeling.cpp \
